{"id": "9th-u3-q017", "schema_version": "1.0", "kind": "single_choice", "level": "SSLC", "difficulty": "easy", "exam_mappings": ["group_4", "group_2", "group_2a"], "syllabus": {"class": "9", "subject_id": "general_tamil", "term": "full_year", "unit_id": "ta-9th-u3-panpaadu", "lesson_id": "lesson-01-eru-thazhuvuthal", "chapter_id": null, "topic_id": "topic-eru-thazhuvuthal", "subtopic_id": null}, "texts": {"ta": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "பண்டைத் தமிழரின் ஐந்திணைகளில் ஏறு தழுவுதல் நிகழ்ந்த முல்லை நிலத்தின் கடவுள் மற்றும் மக்கள் முறையே யார்?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "மாயோன் ; ஆயர், ஆய்ச்சியர்", "B": "முருகன் ; குறவர், குறத்தியர்", "C": "இந்திரன் ; உழவர், உழத்தியர்", "D": "வருணன் ; பரதவர், பரத்தியர்"}, "explanation": "முல்லை நிலத்திற்குரிய தெய்வம் மாயோன் (திருமால்); மக்கள் ஆயர், ஆய்ச்சியர் (இடையர், இடைச்சியர்). இவர்களின் வாழ்வியலோடு ஏறு தழுவுதல் பின்னிப்பிணைந்தது."}, "en": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "In the Sangam landscape taxonomy, who are the presiding deity and inhabitants of the Mullai tract?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "Maayon (Vishnu) ; Aayar and Aaychiyar", "B": "Murugan ; Kuravar and Kuratthiyar", "C": "Indhiran ; Uzhavar and Uzhatthiyar", "D": "Varunan ; Bharathavar and Bharatthiyar"}, "explanation": "Mullai (pastoral forest) is consecrated to Maayon, with Aayar and Aaychiyar forming its pastoral society."}}, "question_data": {"assertion": null, "reason": null, "statements": [], "matching_pairs": [], "ordered_items": [], "numeric_answer": null, "passage_reference": null, "table_reference": null, "image_reference": null}, "answer": {"correct_key": "A", "accepted_keys": ["A"], "correct_order": [], "matching_answer": [], "numeric_value": null, "explanation_key": null}, "question_settings": {"is_negative_question": false, "marks": 1.5, "negative_marks": 0.0, "allow_multiple_answers": false}, "source": {"type": "book", "book_name": "Tamil Nadu Samacheer Kalvi", "publisher": "Tamil Nadu Textbook and Educational Services Corporation", "class": "9", "term": "full_year", "edition": "2024-2025", "page": 50, "chapter": null, "section": null, "reference": "9th Tamil, Unit 1, Page 50", "url": null, "source_notes": null}, "previous_year": {"is_previous_year": false, "exam": null, "exam_name": null, "year": null, "paper": null, "session": null}, "media": {"has_media": false, "items": []}, "tags": ["9th_tamil", "iyal_3", "eru_thazhuvuthal", "sanga_ilakkiyam"], "language_status": {"ta": "available", "en": "available"}, "workflow": {"status": "published", "verification_status": "verified", "created_by": "admin", "created_at": "2026-11-04T09:50:00Z", "updated_at": "2026-11-04T09:50:00Z"}, "version": {"current": 1, "previous_version_id": null, "revision_reason": null}}
{"id": "9th-u3-q018", "schema_version": "1.0", "kind": "statement_analysis", "level": "SSLC", "difficulty": "medium", "exam_mappings": ["group_4", "group_2", "group_2a"], "syllabus": {"class": "9", "subject_id": "general_tamil", "term": "full_year", "unit_id": "ta-9th-u3-panpaadu", "lesson_id": "lesson-01-eru-thazhuvuthal", "chapter_id": null, "topic_id": "topic-eru-thazhuvuthal", "subtopic_id": null}, "texts": {"ta": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "ஏறு தழுவுதல் குறித்த பின்வரும் கூற்றுகளில் தவறானது எது?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "ஏறு தழுவுதல் முல்லை, மருத நிலங்களில் கால் கொண்டு தமிழர்தம் வாழ்வோடு பின்னிப் பிணைந்தது", "B": "ஏறு தழுவுதல் என்பது சங்க காலத்தில் வணிகர்கள் செல்வம் ஈட்டுவதற்காக மட்டுமே நடத்தப்பட்டது", "C": "வீரத்திற்கும் விளைச்சலுக்கும் செழிப்பிற்கும் மாடுகள் அடையாளப்படுத்தப்பட்டன", "D": "கலித்தொகையில் காளைகளின் பாய்ச்சலும் இளைஞர்களின் வீரமும் தத்ரூபமாக விவரிக்கப்பட்டுள்ளன"}, "explanation": "கூற்று B தவறானது. ஏறு தழுவுதல் என்பது வணிகர்கள் செல்வம் ஈட்டும் நிகழ்வு அன்று; இது இளைஞர்களின் வீரத்தையும் தமிழரின் பண்பாட்டையும் வெளிப்படுத்தும் தூய வாழ்வியல் நிகழ்வாகும்."}, "en": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "Which of the following assertions regarding ancient Eru Thazhuvuthal is INCORRECT?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "Eru Thazhuvuthal originated rooted in Mullai and Marutham landscapes", "B": "Eru Thazhuvuthal was organized exclusively by merchants solely to generate trade wealth", "C": "Bulls symbolized chivalry, agricultural harvest, and prosperity", "D": "Kalithogai realistically depicts the furious charge of bulls and youthful bravery"}, "explanation": "Statement B is entirely false; bull taming was an organic pastoral-agrarian folk celebration of valor and love, not a mercantile commercial venture."}}, "question_data": {"assertion": null, "reason": null, "statements": [], "matching_pairs": [], "ordered_items": [], "numeric_answer": null, "passage_reference": null, "table_reference": null, "image_reference": null}, "answer": {"correct_key": "B", "accepted_keys": ["B"], "correct_order": [], "matching_answer": [], "numeric_value": null, "explanation_key": null}, "question_settings": {"is_negative_question": false, "marks": 1.5, "negative_marks": 0.0, "allow_multiple_answers": false}, "source": {"type": "book", "book_name": "Tamil Nadu Samacheer Kalvi", "publisher": "Tamil Nadu Textbook and Educational Services Corporation", "class": "9", "term": "full_year", "edition": "2024-2025", "page": 50, "chapter": null, "section": null, "reference": "9th Tamil, Unit 1, Page 50", "url": null, "source_notes": null}, "previous_year": {"is_previous_year": false, "exam": null, "exam_name": null, "year": null, "paper": null, "session": null}, "media": {"has_media": false, "items": []}, "tags": ["9th_tamil", "iyal_3", "eru_thazhuvuthal", "sanga_ilakkiyam"], "language_status": {"ta": "available", "en": "available"}, "workflow": {"status": "published", "verification_status": "verified", "created_by": "admin", "created_at": "2026-11-04T09:50:00Z", "updated_at": "2026-11-04T09:50:00Z"}, "version": {"current": 1, "previous_version_id": null, "revision_reason": null}}
